  "id": "bharatanatyam_nattuvangam",
  "name": "Bharatanatyam music (nattuvangam margam ensemble)",
  "family": "classical",
  "lineage": "Bharatanatyam, the classical dance of Tamil Nadu that grew out of sadir, the dance of temple and court dancers, is accompanied by a Carnatic ensemble led by the nattuvanar, who recites rhythmic syllables (sollukattu) and keeps time on small cymbals (nattuvangam; the manjira card stands in for them), with a vocalist, mridangam, violin and flute. The margam, the concert order running from alarippu and jatiswaram through varnam and padam to tillana, was codified by the Tanjore Quartet, four brothers at the Thanjavur court in the early nineteenth century.",
